---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="XRP NO BALL GAMES | XRP KIDs, Alpha Aaron & XRPL Lore"
  description="A concise XRP NO BALL GAMES summary covering XRP KIDs, Alpha Aaron, FRET, $PMSL, Block Buster OG and the 100 / 89 / 11 canon with strict verification warnings."
  current="xrp"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">XRP NO BALL GAMES</span>
    <h1>The XRPL branch of the NO BALL GAMES universe.</h1>
    <p>
      This page summarises XRP NO BALL GAMES, XRP KIDs, Alpha Aaron, FRET, $PMSL and Block Buster OG as a lore and digital-collectible branch of the wider brand. Treat issuer, collection and token specifics as unverified until checked against official project records or XRPL ledger data.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Clean public summary</span>
      <h2>Street culture, XRPL myth, anti-control story.</h2>
      <p>
        XRP NO BALL GAMES takes the sign-flip energy of the main brand and pushes it into an XRPL-side story world where collectibles, AI corruption, underground resistance and hidden archive doors all collide.
      </p>
      <p>
        The page stays concise on purpose. The long-form canon lives in the research vault.
      </p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}research/`}>Open the truth archive →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Hard disclaimer</span>
      <h2>Verify before you interact.</h2>
      <p>
        Verify issuer addresses, collection records, token details, NFT pages and marketplace links before interacting with anything presented as XRPL-related. Nothing here is financial advice, and lore should not be mistaken for verified ledger fact.
      </p>
      <div class="coming-soon-tag">Nothing here is financial advice</div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Canon anchors</h2>
      <p>The major names and roles in the XRP-side archive.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">XRP KIDs</span>
        <h3>The genesis set</h3>
        <p>XRP KIDs is the central collectible group in this branch: a 100-piece genesis canon tied to rebellion, humour, play and street-coded memory.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Alpha Aaron</span>
        <h3>The capture logic</h3>
        <p>Alpha Aaron is the antagonist — a corrupted collector and anti-play machine that absorbs culture, centralises ownership and pushes the archive toward control.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">FRET</span>
        <h3>Fresh Rapid Elite Team</h3>
        <p>FRET is the resistance layer: artists, coders, collectors, AR taggers and signal runners organising from the Barbican and the hidden routes of the city.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">$PMSL</span>
        <h3>The hard-fork shield</h3>
        <p>$PMSL belongs to the internal canon as the protective token/lore shield wrapped around the remaining free KIDs. Any live token mechanics still need ledger proof.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Block Buster OG</span>
        <h3>The hidden 1/1 archive key</h3>
        <p>Block Buster OG is the hidden intervention layer: part Charlie Buster memory archive, part anti-Alpha system, part mythic door-opener inside the story world.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Locked counts</span>
      <h2>100 / 89 / 11</h2>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li><strong>100 genesis KIDs</strong> form the starting canon.</li>
        <li><strong>89 captured</strong> marks Alpha Aaron's takeover phase.</li>
        <li><strong>11 free</strong> remain the emotional core of the resistance and the $PMSL shield mythology.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These counts are part of the lore baseline and should be labelled as canon until matching public records are attached.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Truth guard</span>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li>Do not invent issuer addresses, wallet details, collection IDs or floor prices.</li>
        <li>Do not present lore events as verified real-world history.</li>
        <li>Do not treat a ticker alone as proof of identity on XRPL.</li>
        <li>Check official records before describing any token, NFT or marketplace interaction.</li>
        <li>Use the research vault if you need the long-form canon or source-needed notes.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-block">
    <div class="cta-block-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Need the long version?</span>
      <h2>Read the archive, then ask the right question.</h2>
      <p>The research vault holds the full truth baseline. The contact page is the place for collector, lore and source-check enquiries.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}research/`}>Read the truth file index</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}contact/`}>Contact the archive</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
